Description: Makefile: link the libraries V\OS ships
 Upstream lists "media midi game network translation tracker debug" in
 LIBS. V\OS ships none of -lmedia, -lmidi, -lnetwork and -ldebug: its
 media kit is libmedia2.so (play_sound lives there), the legacy endpoint
 network library was dropped in favour of POSIX sockets (which this app
 already uses directly), and there is no midi or debugger kit library.
 -lgame also goes: the app never calls the joystick kit. What stays: be
 (kits), media2 (play_sound, replacing media), translation
 (BTranslationUtils::GetBitmap) and tracker -- V\OS puts BFilePanel in
 libtracker, and the link fails without it. -lroot is exported by the
 vos_makefile_engine buildsystem class; STDCPPLIBS was already listed by
 upstream.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/

---
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS =  $(STDCPPLIBS) be media midi game network translation tracker debug
+LIBS =  $(STDCPPLIBS) be media2 translation tracker
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
